+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value |
+| ------ | ----- |
+| Issue  | #37   |
+| Status | Draft |
+
+`ToolRegistry.execute` validates a tool call's `input` against the resolved definition's `inputSchema` before the executor runs. A rejection is returned as a `ToolResponse`, so the model can read it and correct the call within the tool-round bound; only an unknown tool name throws.
+
+## Contract
+
+- Input that fails the schema returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` names the missing property, and the executor is never invoked ([validated by: rejects input missing a required property](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L27)).
+- Valid input carrying a property the schema does not list reaches the executor unchanged, exactly once; nothing is defaulted, coerced or stripped ([validated by: passes valid input with an unlisted extra property](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L39)).
+- A wrong-typed field is rejected with a message naming its path and the expected type, never the offending value; no log line carries the value either ([validated by: rejects a wrong-typed field](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L57)).
+- A schema that cannot be compiled makes `register` throw, with a message naming the tool ([validated by: throws at register time](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L80)).
+- A function-valued definition is resolved on every call and validated against the schema current at that call ([validated by: validates a function-valued definition](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L87)).
